  33:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * This driver has been tested with the following MCUs:
  34:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *  - F070, F072, L053, F042F6
  35:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
  36:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * It also should work with minimal changes for any ST MCU with an "USB A"/"PCD"/"HCD" peripheral. 
  37:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *  covers:
  38:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
  39:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * F04x, F072, F078, F070x6/B     1024 byte buffer
  40:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * F102, F103                      512 byte buffer; no internal D+ pull-up (maybe many more changes
  41:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * F302xB/C, F303xB/C, F373        512 byte buffer; no internal D+ pull-up
  42:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * F302x6/8, F302xD/E2, F303xD/E  1024 byte buffer; no internal D+ pull-up
  43:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * C0                             2048 byte buffer; 32-bit bus; host mode
  44:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * G0                             2048 byte buffer; 32-bit bus; host mode
  45:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * G4                             1024 byte buffer
  46:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * H5                             2048 byte buffer; 32-bit bus; host mode
  47:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * L0x2, L0x3                     1024 byte buffer
  48:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * L1                              512 byte buffer
  49:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * L4x2, L4x3                     1024 byte buffer
  50:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * L5                             1024 byte buffer
  51:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * U0                             1024 byte buffer; 32-bit bus
  52:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * U535, U545                     2048 byte buffer; 32-bit bus; host mode
  53:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * WB35, WB55                     1024 byte buffer
  54:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
  55:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * To use this driver, you must:
  56:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - If you are using a device with crystal-less USB, set up the clock recovery system (CRS)
  57:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - Remap pins to be D+/D- on devices that they are shared (for example: F042Fx)
  58:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *   - This is different to the normal "alternate function" GPIO interface, needs to go through SYS
  59:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - Enable USB clock; Perhaps use __HAL_RCC_USB_CLK_ENABLE();
  60:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - (Optionally configure GPIO HAL to tell it the USB driver is using the USB pins)
  61:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - call tusb_init();
  62:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - periodically call tusb_task();
  63:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
  64:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * Assumptions of the driver:
  65:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - You are not using CAN (it must share the packet buffer)
  66:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - APB clock is >= 10 MHz
  67:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - On some boards, series resistors are required, but not on others.
  68:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - On some boards, D+ pull up resistor (1.5kohm) is required, but not on others.
  69:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - You don't have long-running interrupts; some USB packets must be quickly responded to.
  70:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - You have the ST CMSIS library linked into the project. HAL is not used.
  71:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
  72:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * Current driver limitations (i.e., a list of features for you to add):
  73:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - STALL handled, but not tested.
  74:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *   - Does it work? No clue.
  75:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - All EP BTABLE buffers are created based on max packet size of first EP opened with that addres
  76:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - Packet buffer memory is copied in the interrupt.
  77:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *   - This is better for performance, but means interrupts are disabled for longer
  78:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *   - DMA may be the best choice, but it could also be pushed to the USBD task.
  79:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - No double-buffering
  80:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - No DMA
  81:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - Minimal error handling
  82:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *   - Perhaps error interrupts should be reported to the stack, or cause a device reset?
  83:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - Assumes a single USB peripheral; I think that no hardware has multiple so this is fine.
  84:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - Add a callback for enabling/disabling the D+ PU on devices without an internal PU.
  85:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - F3 models use three separate interrupts. I think we could only use the LP interrupt for
  86:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *     everything?  However, the interrupts are configurable so the DisableInt and EnableInt
  87:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *     below functions could be adjusting the wrong interrupts (if they had been reconfigured)
  88:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - LPM is not used correctly, or at all?
  89:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
