  97:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
  98:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - YouTube OpenTechLab 011; https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4FOkJLp_PUw
  99:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
 100:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * Advantages over HAL driver:
 101:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - Tiny (saves RAM, assumes a single USB peripheral)
 102:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *
 103:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * Notes:
 104:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  * - The buffer table is allocated as endpoints are opened. The allocation is only
 105:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *   cleared when the device is reset. This may be bad if the USB device needs
 106:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  *   to be reconfigured.
 107:tinyusb/src/portable/st/stm32_fsdev/dcd_stm32_fsdev.c ****  */
